.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt LANDSTRIP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm landstrip
.Nd run commands inside an OS-level sandbox
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Cm run
.Op Fl p Ar file
.Op Fl -policy-format Ar format
.Op Fl -cwd Ar dir
.Op Fl -trap Ar FD|PATH
.Op Fl -inherit Ar FD[,FD...]
.Op Fl -
.Ar program
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sandboxes programs using JSON or YAML policies in a supported subset of the
Anthropic Sandbox Runtime format.
Execute commands under the merged policy with the
.Cm run
subcommand.
Use
.Nm Ar command Fl -help
for command help.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "windows prepare-appcontainer"
.It Cm run
Execute a sandboxed program under the merged policy.
.It Cm check
Check parsing, paths, executable policy, and platform support.
.It Cm resolve
Print the normalized merged policy as JSON.
.It Cm doctor
Report sandbox health and supported/available capabilities as JSON.
.It Cm windows install
Install restricted-user isolation; requires elevation.
.It Cm windows prepare-appcontainer
Prepare null-device and root directory lookup access for standard AppContainer
and LPAC; requires elevation and verifies both modes.
.It Cm windows status
Report the active implementation and its health.
.It Cm windows uninstall
Remove restricted-user isolation and return to AppContainer.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss General
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -debug
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help.
.El
.Ss Policy input
For
.Cm run ,
.Cm check ,
and
.Cm resolve :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar file , Fl -policy Ar file
Read a policy; repeat to merge files.
Use
.Sq -
for stdin with
.Fl -policy-format .
.It Fl -policy-format Ar format
Select
.Va json
or
.Va yaml .
.It Fl -cwd Ar dir
Set the working directory for policy resolution and execution
(defaults to the current working directory).
On Unix, relative executable paths and relative or empty
.Ev PATH
entries also use this directory when locating executable policy.
Paths passed to
.Fl -policy
remain relative to the caller's working directory.
.It Fl -tool Ar program
Include the resolved executable's policy when validating or resolving.
.El
.Ss Run descriptors
Unix (Linux/macOS) only; supplied descriptors must be open, distinct, and
numbered 3 or higher.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -trap Ar FD|PATH
Use an inherited open descriptor or an absolute Unix domain stream socket path;
not repeatable.
For a path, the host Landstrip process connects to an existing listener before
sandbox setup.
The sandboxed program never inherits the trap transport.
On Linux the stream is bidirectional and uses the existing broker query/response
protocol, not merely passive monitoring.
macOS reports only setup/launch failures and closes it on successful exec.
See
.Sx OUTPUT .
.It Fl -inherit Ar FD[,FD...]
Preserve a comma-separated descriptor list across exec; repeat to append.
Duplicates and overlap with
.Fl -trap
are rejected.
Inherited descriptors bypass pathname/network policy for their resources.
Other descriptors except stdin, stdout, and stderr are closed before exec.
.El
.Ss Windows installation
For
.Cm windows install :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -restricted-accounts Ar count
Set the restricted-network account pool size.
.It Fl -unrestricted-accounts Ar count
Set the unrestricted-network account pool size.
.It Fl -proxy-port-range Ar low-high
Set the loopback port range restricted-user sandboxes may reach.
.El
.Sh POLICY
Policies and their filesystem sections must be objects.
When multiple policy documents are given, sections merge recursively, list
entries are appended without duplicates, and later documents override non-list
fields; executable policy is merged last.
Hard-denial roots
.Pq Va denyReadAlways No and Va denyWriteAlways
accumulate across documents, including newline-string lists;
empty/null values cannot clear earlier roots.
.Pp
Example fields, subject to the platform limits below:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "filesystem": {
    "allowWrite": ["."], "denyWrite": ["**/.env"],
    "denyWriteAlways": ["~/vault/secrets"],
    "denyRead": ["~/.ssh"], "allowRead": ["~/.ssh/config"],
    "denyReadAlways": ["~/.config/agent/auth.json"]
  },
  "network": {
    "allowNetwork": false, "allowLocalBinding": false,
    "httpProxyPort": 8080, "socksProxyPort": 8081,
    "allowUnixSockets": [], "allowAllUnixSockets": false,
    "supervisorSockets": null
  },
  "macos": {
    "allowTrustd": false, "allowMachLookup": [],
    "allowAppleEvents": false, "allowPty": false,
    "logTag": "agent-session-42"
  },
  "windows": { "appContainerMode": "lpac", "allowLoopback": false,
               "allowAdditiveGrants": false }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Relative paths resolve against
.Fl -cwd
(default: current working directory);
.Sq ~
expands to the user's home directory.
Relative
.Va denyWrite
and
.Va denyWriteAlways
entries additionally anchor at every
.Va allowWrite
root that is a directory, so the write deny list covers all granted write
scopes, not only the policy base.
Relative
.Va denyWriteAlways
entries also match each granted root's own name, protecting exact-file grants
and directory roots that match the deny selector.
Path entries accept bare strings, explicit literal selectors
.Pq Dq literal ,
or explicit glob selectors
.Pq Dq glob .
Path globs follow the platform path syntax: a single
.Va *
or
.Va \&?
never spans a path separator, a double asterisk followed by a separator also
matches zero directories
.Po so
.Dq **/.env
covers the granted root itself
.Pc ,
and Windows matching is case-insensitive.
.Ss Filesystem
Writes default to denied.
.Va allowWrite
grants roots and adds exceptions to
.Va denyWrite ,
with the most specific rule winning;
.Va denyWriteAlways
cannot be overridden by grants or broker approval.
Reads default to unrestricted on Linux/macOS and require explicit
.Va allowRead
grants on Windows.
.Va allowRead
adds exceptions to
.Va denyRead ,
but never
.Va denyReadAlways .
A write root nested inside a
.Va denyRead
root stays writable, because
.Va denyRead
removes read access only.
Protected roots and descendants stay denied across moves, hard links,
canonical symlink aliases, and broker approval.
Denied roots and descendants also cannot be removed.
Linux/macOS enforce concrete and glob read/write denials at access time;
Windows enforces only concrete non-root paths existing at startup and rejects
nonempty
.Va denyReadAlways
and
.Va denyWriteAlways .
.Ss Network
Direct TCP/UDP is denied by default.
Linux/macOS proxy ports permit loopback TCP to those ports without starting
a proxy.
.Va allowLocalBinding
permits host-local TCP/UDP binding and connections, not remote UDP.
.Va allowUnixSockets
permits listed pathname sockets and
.Va allowAllUnixSockets
permits all pathname Unix sockets, independently of
.Va allowNetwork .
Windows supports neither local binding nor Unix socket policy.
AppContainer permits loopback TCP to the declared proxy ports.
Restricted-user mode adds per-run loopback permits for the same ports, so an
undeclared port stays closed even inside the installed proxy port range.
.Va allowNetwork
permits general IP networking without relaxing Unix socket, filesystem, or
escape-prevention rules.
.Pp
Linux keeps service manager sockets denied even under
.Va allowAllUnixSockets :
approving one would start a process outside the sandbox.
The default set is discovered from
.Ev DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS ,
.Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS ,
and
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
falling back to
.Pa /run/dbus/system_bus_socket ,
.Pa /run/systemd ,
and
.Pa /run/user/<uid> .
.Va supervisorSockets
replaces that set, so a policy naming its own service manager is not also
restricted to this host's sockets.
.Ss Platform enforcement
.Bl -tag -width Windows
.It Linux
Commands run in new user, PID, and mount namespaces with a private procfs and
a PID-1 reaper that forwards termination signals and reaps all descendants
on exit.
Landlock enforces filesystem roots; seccomp brokers network/filesystem traps
and blocks service-manager sockets and io_uring.
Linux 6.12+ also restricts abstract Unix sockets and signals outside
the sandbox.
.It macOS
Seatbelt fixes the profile at startup.
.Va macos.allowTrustd ,
.Va macos.allowMachLookup
(exact service names or
.Sq *
prefix wildcards),
.Va macos.allowAppleEvents ,
and
.Va macos.allowPty
grant the corresponding IPC or pseudo-terminal access.
The optional
.Va macos.logTag
string tags Seatbelt denial logs for correlation.
It must be nonempty and contain no double quote, backslash, ASCII control
character (0x00-0x1f), or DEL (0x7f).
The JSON section remains
.Va macos ,
not
.Va darwin .
.Dv AF_ROUTE
sockets remain available for route/interface discovery.
.It Windows
Uses AppContainer
.Pq Va lpac No default or Va standard
or restricted users with Windows Filtering Platform.
.Va windows.allowLoopback
exposes local loopback services in AppContainer mode.
Restricted-user accounts reach loopback only for the proxy ports their policy
declares, all of which must lie inside the installed proxy port range.
A restricted-user account keeps its own
.Sq Users
rights, so
.Va allowRead
and
.Va allowWrite
permits are additive rather than an allowlist.
Landstrip refuses such a policy unless
.Va windows.allowAdditiveGrants
is set.
If AppContainer cannot open
.Pa NUL ,
run
.Cm landstrip windows prepare-appcontainer
from an interactive session after reboot to grant non-inheritable null-device
and root lookup access to AppContainer package SIDs.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
Policy, doctor, and Windows management commands write one JSON document
to stdout.
Failures and reported Linux broker denials are JSON lines on stderr with stable
.Va kind
.Pq Va filesystem , network , launch , usage , internal
and
.Va code
fields.
Linux explicit read denials
.Pq Dv DenyMatch , Va reason No set to Dq deny_match
are reported even when the program exits 0.
.Fl -trap
receives these events except usage errors.
Linux approval queries require a bidirectional stream socket on
.Fl -trap ;
reply with a JSON line containing the unchanged
.Va query_id
and
.Va action
.Pq Dq allow No or Dq deny .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Program execution returns the program's status after terminating and reaping
any remaining Linux sandbox descendants.
Other failures, including invalid policies and unhealthy reports, return 1;
usage errors return 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
landstrip run -p policy.json -- cargo test
landstrip check -p - --policy-format yaml < policy.yaml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://github.com/landstrip/landstrip#readme
